    "content": "<!-- wp:cil/page-head {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"title\":\"Children and teenagers circumcision - from £300\",\"lede\":\"Circumcision can make both a child and his parents feel anxious, particularly when a child is old enough to understand that he is having a procedure.\",\"reviewedBy\":\"<a href=\\\"/team/#haidar\\\">Dr Haidar Al-Ali, BDS, MFDS RCPS (Glasg)</a>, September 2026\",\"reviewedLabel\":\"Clinically reviewed by\",\"homeLabel\":\"Home\",\"crumbs\":[{\"label\":\"Who we see\",\"href\":\"/babies/\"},{\"label\":\"Children and teenagers\",\"href\":\"\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-sky\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"overview\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-sky\" id=\"overview\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false,\"bleed\":true} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split split--bleed\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cil-split-copy\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cil-split-copy\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Circumcision can make both a child and his parents feel anxious, particularly when a child is old enough to understand that he is having a procedure.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At Beverley Clinic in North-West London, we provide circumcision for boys and teenagers for religious, cultural, personal and medical reasons. Our practitioners have extensive experience treating children of different ages and understand that the way we approach a five-year-old should be very different from the way we speak to a teenager.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our aim is to make the experience as calm and straightforward as possible. Before the appointment, we provide preparation information so that parents know what to expect and how to prepare their son without giving him unnecessary information that may increase his anxiety.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The procedure is performed using local anaesthetic. For older children and teenagers, we commonly use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"children-boys\",\"alt\":\"Two young boys playing together outdoors.\",\"ratio\":\"4-3\"} /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:cil/split -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/spec-panel {\"eyebrow\":\"At a glance\",\"rows\":[{\"k\":\"Age\",\"v\":\"Children and teenagers\"},{\"k\":\"Common method\",\"v\":\"Forceps-guided (traditional) with thermal cautery\"},{\"k\":\"Anaesthetic\",\"v\":\"Local anaesthetic\"},{\"k\":\"Closure\",\"v\":\"Skin glue, dissolvable stitches, both, or occasionally neither\"},{\"k\":\"School letters\",\"v\":\"Ask the clinic if needed\"},{\"k\":\"Price\",\"v\":\"From £300, depending on age\"}],\"note\":\"From £300, depending on age. See the <a href=\\\"/prices/\\\" style=\\\"color:var(--blue-deep)\\\">full price list</a>, broken down by age band.\"} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"preparation\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"preparation\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Preparation\",\"heading\":\"How should I prepare my child for circumcision?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>One of the most common questions parents ask us is how much they should tell their child.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our advice is to keep the explanation very minimal and appropriate for your child's age.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Young children usually do not benefit from a detailed description of every stage of the procedure. Too much information given too early can sometimes increase anxiety. Mentioning words like injection or cutting only scares the child and may make them uncooperative for us to carry out the circumcision.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You might simply explain that you are going to a clinic where we will do some cleaning, and that you will be there to support him.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Older children and teenagers will naturally have more questions and should be involved in the discussion in a way that is appropriate for their age and understanding.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our practitioners are accustomed to speaking directly to children and teenagers. We can explain what is going to happen calmly on the day and answer their questions before anything begins.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"appointment-walkthrough\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"appointment-walkthrough\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"On the day\",\"heading\":\"What happens at the appointment?\",\"lede\":\"The appointment involves more than the circumcision itself. We allow time for registration, local anaesthetic, the procedure and explaining the aftercare.\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/steps {\"items\":[{\"h\":\"1. Registration and consent\",\"p\":\"We check the required identification and consent and medical history information. Please tell us in advance about any medical conditions, medication, allergies or previous problems with bleeding.\"},{\"h\":\"2. Examination\",\"p\":\"Your son is examined before the circumcision. We assess the penis and foreskin and look for anything that may influence how the procedure should be performed, including phimosis, scarring, BXO (lichen sclerosis), a tight frenulum or buried penis. If we identify something that means routine circumcision is not appropriate, we will explain this rather than simply proceeding.\"},{\"h\":\"3. Local anaesthetic\",\"p\":\"Local anaesthetic is given around the penis and allowed time to work. We check the area before beginning the circumcision.\"},{\"h\":\"4. Circumcision\",\"p\":\"For most older children and teenagers, we use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery. The foreskin is carefully positioned and a specialist surgical forceps is used to guide the circumcision and protect the underlying structures. Thermal cautery helps control bleeding during the procedure. Depending on your son's age, anatomy and the wound following circumcision, the skin may be closed using dissolvable stitches, medical skin glue, a combination of both, or occasionally neither.\"},{\"h\":\"5. Aftercare\",\"p\":\"After the procedure, your son can put his underwear and trousers back on and walk normally. Before you leave, we explain how to look after the circumcision, what to expect during healing and when to contact us. You will also receive written aftercare instructions.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-children-aftercare\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-children-aftercare is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href=\"/aftercare/\">Read our circumcision aftercare information →</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"anaesthetic-and-comfort\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"anaesthetic-and-comfort\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":true,\"bleed\":true} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split reverse split--bleed\"><!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"treatment-room\",\"alt\":\"The clean, white treatment room at the Edgware clinic, with a treatment couch.\",\"ratio\":\"4-3\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cil-split-copy\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cil-split-copy\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Patient comfort\",\"heading\":\"Is general anaesthetic necessary for child circumcision?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>At our clinic, circumcision for suitable children and teenagers is performed using local anaesthetic rather than routine general anaesthetic.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This means your son remains awake during the procedure.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Local anaesthetic is administered around the penis and given time to work before we begin. We check that the area is adequately anaesthetised before proceeding.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not every child is suitable for a procedure under local anaesthetic. Age alone does not determine this — we also consider the child's maturity, anxiety, ability to cooperate and individual circumstances.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If we do not believe it is appropriate or safe to proceed under local anaesthetic, we will tell you.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:cil/split -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"icon\":\"heart\",\"eyebrow\":\"Sensation & Reassurance\",\"title\":\"Will my child feel the circumcision?\",\"html\":\"<p>Local anaesthetic is used to numb the area before the circumcision begins.</p><p>A child may still be aware that something is happening and may notice movement, touch or pressure even when the area has been anaesthetised.</p><p>Children can also become upset because they are anxious, in an unfamiliar environment or dislike being examined or held still.</p><p>Although most children cooperate really well with the way we do the circumcision, we avoid promising parents that a child will experience absolutely no discomfort. Instead, our aim is to make sure the local anaesthetic has had time to work and to keep your son as comfortable and reassured as possible throughout the procedure.</p>\"},{\"icon\":\"users\",\"eyebrow\":\"Parent support\",\"title\":\"Can I stay with my child?\",\"html\":\"<p>We understand that having a procedure can be stressful for both children and parents.</p><p>We allow one parent to be present with the child inside the surgery room.</p><p>After the circumcision, a member of staff will make sure you understand the aftercare before you leave.</p>\"}]} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"what-to-bring\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"what-to-bring\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Appointment preparation\",\"heading\":\"What should we bring to the appointment?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"waiting-room\",\"alt\":\"The clinic waiting area, with adult seating and a small blue child's chair.\",\"caption\":\"The waiting area. Bring whatever keeps him occupied.\",\"ratio\":\"4-3\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-children-wear\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-children-wear is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">What should my child wear?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We recommend comfortable clothing that is easy to put on after the procedure.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Loose trousers or tracksuit bottoms can be more comfortable than tight jeans immediately afterwards.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We recommend tight well fitting and supportive underwear to wear during the healing period such as tight V shaped briefs. This can be useful for older boys and teenagers because it holds the penis upright and reduces unnecessary movement of the penis to minimise swelling.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-children-bring\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-children-bring is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">Please bring:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} -->\n<ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>The identification and consent documents requested by the clinic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Details of any medication your son takes</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Relevant medical letters if he has an existing medical condition</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Comfortable underwear and loose-fitting trousers or tracksuit bottoms</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Something familiar to keep him occupied, such as a tablet, headphones, book or handheld game</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For younger children, bringing a favourite toy or familiar activity can make waiting much easier.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If only one parent will attend, or there are different parental-responsibility arrangements such as single parents, contact us before the appointment so that we can explain the documents and consent required.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text is-style-cil-card cil-children-duration\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-style-cil-card cil-children-duration is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">How long does child circumcision take?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The circumcision is usually only 10-20 minutes depending on the age, size of the penis and the patient's cooperation.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"healing-and-recovery\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"healing-and-recovery\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Healing & Recovery\",\"heading\":\"What does normal healing look like?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The penis will look different immediately after circumcision, and its appearance changes during healing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group body-text is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Some redness, swelling, bruising and sensitivity can occur after the procedure. The head of the penis may also initially appear particularly sensitive because it was previously covered by the foreskin.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Parents are sometimes concerned simply because they have never seen a circumcision wound healing before.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We explain what to expect and provide written aftercare instructions. If you are unsure whether something you are seeing is normal, contact us and ask.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Wound closure\",\"title\":\"What happens to the stitches after circumcision?\",\"html\":\"<p>Where stitches are required, we normally use dissolvable stitches, so they do not usually need to be removed.</p><p>The stitches gradually loosen and disappear as healing progresses.</p><p>Medical skin glue may also be used, either instead of stitches or in combination with them, depending on the wound.</p>\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Comfort at home\",\"title\":\"Will my child need pain relief afterwards?\",\"html\":\"<p>Some soreness or discomfort during the early healing period is expected after a surgical procedure.</p><p>We will discuss appropriate pain relief with you before you leave the clinic.</p><p>Any medication should be given according to the instructions appropriate for your child's age and weight.</p><p>Do not give your child medication simply because another parent was advised to use it following their child's circumcision. Follow the instructions provided for your son.</p>\"}]} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"school-and-sports\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"school-and-sports\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Activity & Lifestyle\",\"heading\":\"When can my child return to school and sports?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"icon\":\"calendar\",\"eyebrow\":\"Classroom\",\"title\":\"When can my child return to school?\",\"html\":\"<p>This depends on your child's age, how he feels and the type of activities he normally does at school.</p><p>Some children are comfortable returning after 2 weeks, while others benefit from additional time at home.</p><p>We can provide a school letter where appropriate.</p><p>When your son returns, his school may need to know that he should temporarily avoid activities that could place pressure or friction on the healing area.</p>\"},{\"icon\":\"clock\",\"eyebrow\":\"Physical activity\",\"title\":\"When can my child return to PE, football and sports?\",\"html\":\"<p>Returning to the classroom and returning to sport are not necessarily the same thing.</p><p>Your son may feel comfortable walking and attending school before the circumcision has healed enough for PE, football, cycling, swimming, martial arts or contact sports.</p><p>Activities involving running, jumping or lifting should be avoided until the wound has healed sufficiently.</p><p>We will give you individual advice following the procedure about when these activities can gradually be resumed.</p>\"},{\"icon\":\"users\",\"eyebrow\":\"Teenagers\",\"title\":\"What about erections in teenagers?\",\"html\":\"<p>Teenagers may naturally experience erections during the healing period, including during sleep or on waking.</p><p>An erection can temporarily cause pulling or tightness around a healing circumcision wound and stitches. This can be uncomfortable but does not automatically mean that something has gone wrong.</p><p>We discuss the healing process privately and appropriately with teenage patients and explain when they should contact us if they are concerned.</p>\"}]} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-sky\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"medical-reasons\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-sky\" id=\"medical-reasons\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Medical reasons\",\"heading\":\"Circumcision for medical conditions in children\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Tight foreskin\",\"title\":\"Circumcision for a tight foreskin in children\",\"html\":\"<p>A foreskin that does not retract in a young boy is not automatically abnormal.</p><p>The foreskin naturally separates from the head of the penis as a child develops, and this process can continue for many years. Parents should never forcibly retract a child's foreskin, as this can cause pain, injury and scarring.</p><p>Circumcision for medical reasons is therefore different from circumcision chosen for religious or cultural reasons.</p><p>If your son has a tight foreskin (phimosis) or difficulty urinating, he may need a circumcision for medical reasons. Please mention this at the time of booking as extra information may be required before the appointment and there maybe additional charges depending on the severity.</p><p><a href=\\\"/conditions/phimosis/\\\">Learn more about phimosis →</a></p>\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Inflammation\",\"title\":\"What if my child has recurrent balanitis?\",\"html\":\"<p>Balanitis is inflammation affecting the head of the penis and can cause redness, soreness, irritation or discharge.</p><p>A single episode does not necessarily mean that a child requires circumcision.</p><p>Where balanitis keeps returning, particularly in association with foreskin tightness or scarring, we can assess your son and offer circumcision as a suitable treatment option.</p><p><a href=\\\"/conditions/balanitis/\\\">Learn more about balanitis →</a></p>\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Foreskin scarring\",\"title\":\"What is BXO?\",\"html\":\"<p>BXO (balanitis xerotica obliterans), also known as male genital lichen sclerosis, is a condition that can cause whitening, thickening and scarring of the foreskin.</p><p>The resulting scar tissue can make the foreskin progressively tighter.</p><p>BXO is different from the normal non-retractile foreskin seen in many younger boys, which is why examination is important when a medical problem is suspected.</p><p>Circumcision may be recommended where BXO significantly affects the foreskin.</p><p><a href=\\\"/conditions/bxo/\\\">Learn more about BXO / lichen sclerosis →</a></p>\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Anatomy\",\"title\":\"What if my child has a buried penis?\",\"html\":\"<p>A buried or hidden penis is where some or all of the penis sits within the surrounding pubic tissue.</p><p>Recognising this before circumcision is important because it can influence both the procedure and the aftercare.</p><p>Our practitioners assess this before proceeding. In most patients with buried penis, we are still able to carry out the circumcision. If for any reason, we are unable, we will inform you and discuss the next appropriate steps.</p>\"}]} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/cta-band {\"title\":\"If you have further questions\",\"text\":\"<p>If you have further questions, you can either <a href=\\\"tel:+442089513794\\\">call us</a> or <a href=\\\"#request-callback\\\">request for us to call you back</a>. You can also send us an email enquiry or speak to us via Whatsapp.</p><p class=\\\"cil-cta-contacts\\\"><a class=\\\"cil-cta-contact cil-cta-contact--email\\\" href=\\\"mailto:info@circumcisioninlondon.co.uk\\\"><span class=\\\"cil-cta-contact__label\\\">Email</span>info@circumcisioninlondon.co.uk</a><a class=\\\"cil-cta-contact cil-cta-contact--whatsapp\\\" href=\\\"https://wa.me/447886779958\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" data-track=\\\"whatsapp-cta\\\"><span class=\\\"cil-cta-contact__label\\\">WhatsApp</span>07886779958</a></p>\",\"eyebrow\":\"Talk to us\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book online\",\"ctaUrl\":\"/book/\",\"phoneLabel\":\"Call 020 8951 3794\",\"phoneUrl\":\"tel:+442089513794\",\"cardTitle\":\"\",\"cardHtml\":\"\",\"cardEyebrow\":\"Request a call back\",\"showCallback\":true,\"formId\":\"children\",\"formSubject\":\"children and teenagers enquiry\",\"callbackAnchor\":\"request-callback\",\"nameLabel\":\"Your name\",\"phoneFieldLabel\":\"Phone number\",\"dobLabel\":\"Patient DOB\",\"messageLabel\":\"Anything you would like us to know\",\"optionalLabel\":\"(optional)\",\"consentHtml\":\"I am happy for the clinic to contact me about this enquiry. We do not add you to a mailing list. See our <a href=\\\"/privacy-notice/\\\" style=\\\"color:var(--blue-deep)\\\">privacy notice</a>.\",\"submitLabel\":\"Request a call back\",\"invalidMessage\":\"Please complete the highlighted field.\",\"sentMessage\":\"Opening your email app so this reaches the clinic. If nothing happens, call 020 8951 3794.\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-sky\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-sky\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Also at this clinic\",\"heading\":\"Circumcision at other ages\",\"lede\":\"\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/group-cards {\"level\":3,\"exclude\":\"/children/\",\"banded\":false,\"items\":[{\"image\":\"home/babies-card-720.webp\",\"imageAlt\":\"\",\"href\":\"/babies/\",\"title\":\"Babies and toddlers\",\"age\":\"Best under one month old\",\"price\":\"From £200\",\"cta\":\"Baby circumcision, from £200\",\"blurb\":\"The ring method, Plastibell or Circumplast, under local anaesthetic. About ten minutes, no stitches, and you take him home straight afterwards. Bath him straight away.\"},{\"image\":\"home/adults-card-720.webp\",\"imageAlt\":\"\",\"href\":\"/adults/\",\"title\":\"Adult men\",\"age\":\"Eighteen and over\",\"price\":\"From £680\",\"cta\":\"Adult circumcision, from £680\",\"blurb\":\"Forceps guided, under local anaesthetic. You stay awake and can talk to the doctor, watch television or listen to music throughout.\"}]} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->"
}
